[[File:E 677.png|thumb|[[Sage of Mind Soractes|Sage of Mind Soractes]], the first example of a Sage]]
'''Sage Enemies''' (超賢者, ''Chō Kenja'', '''Super-Sages''') are a type of enemy introduced in [[Version 13.1 Update|Version 13.1]] and first encountered in [[Garden of Wilted Thoughts]]. Sages have a [[Special Abilities#Resist|resistance]] to all debuffs inflicted by [[Cat Units]], including [[Weaken]], [[Freeze]], [[Knockback]], [[Slow]] and [[Curse]]. Effect durations and knockback distance are reduced by 70%.

The only ability to specifically affect Sages is [[:Category:Sage Slayer Cats|Sage Slayer]], which increases damage against them to 1.2x, reduces damage taken from them to 0.5x, bypasses their debuff resistances and grants the Sage Slayer 70% resistance to debuffs inflicted by Sages, including [[Warp]] and [[Special Abilities#Delay|Drain]].

Like [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]], [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] and [[:Category:Kaijin Enemies|Kaijin]], Sage is not considered a trait, but always overlaps with one of the standard enemy types. All Sage enemies' designs include a shiny blue hexagonal gem.

==Trivia==
*The Sage type was foreshadowed by the [[Uncanny Legends]] ending, in which an ancient god tasks the Cat Army with finding a sage in the [[Legend Stages#Zero Legends|Zero World]].
**[[Golem Sunfish]]'s description may have also served as foreshadowing, claiming it was sealed by a sage, which predated the end of Uncanny Legends by half a year, and the introduction of Sage enemies by close to 2 years.
*The coloration of the Sages' gems may stem from how the color blue is commonly associated with wisdom, intelligence and knowledge.
*Most Sage enemies appears to be based on historical figures or mythology:
