|It's unclear as to whom Tarsiriel is based on, but their debut being the American-themed sub-chapter [[Stratospheric Pathway]] could point it being towards an American historical figure. The focus given to their glasses might allude to [[wikipedia:Benjamin Franklin|Benjamin Franklin]], a Founding Father who invented bifocals, while the closest known match for their design is [[wikipedia:Peter Cooper|Peter Cooper]], an inventor and industrialist best known for creating America's first steam locomotive, ''[[wikipedia:Tom Thumb (locomotive)|Tom Thumb]]''.<br>Tarsiriel also bears a slight resemblance to Brazilian educator and philosopher [[wikipedia:Paulo Freire|Paulo Freire]], and their description and [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/Sage typing may reference [[wikipedia:Saint Peter|St. Peter]], an Apostle of Jesus whose means "stone"; St. Peter is often portrayed as Heaven's gatekeeper and greeter.
