|[[Doctor K.O.]]
|[[wikipedia:Karl Marx|Karl Marx]] (German philosopher and founder of modern communism)
|Similar hairstyle and mustache, is traited as [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]], and the name K.O. starts with a "K". Compared to other [[Kang Roo]] variants, Doctor K.O. has a larger, more curved tail that points upwards, resembling the blade of the sickle in the communist hammer and sickle when flipped horizontally. In [[Pop-pop Wonderland]], Doctor K.O. appears alongside [[CTO Seal]], an enemy from [[Worker's Revolution (Monthly Event)|Worker's Revolution]].
|-
|[[Techn-Old Hyena]]
|[[wikipedia:Albert Einstein|Albert Einstein]] (German-born US theoretical physicist)
|Similar hairstyle and mustache, his [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] trait and Warp ability possibly alluding to Einstein's [[wikipedia:Theory of relativity|theory of relativity]]. The fact that he is a variant of [[H. Nah]] may be a subtle reference to Einstein's formula for [[wikipedia:mass–energy equivalence|mass-energy equivalence]], E=mc^2, as H. Nah's Japanese name is High Energy (ハイ・エナジー).
|-
|[[Oldstrich]]
|[[wikipedia:Leonardo da Vinci|Leonardo da Vinci]] (Italian polymath, painter and engineer)
|The "Da" part of Oldstrich's Japanese name, Da Chōrō (ダ・チョー老), may be derived from da Vinci. Da Vinci was a pioneering anatomist who dissected more than 30 human corpses and extensively studied the skeletal structures, muscles and organs of both humans and other vertebrates, including birds, which may play into Oldstrich's [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] trait. His Toxic ability could allude to how da Vinci [https://www.acs.org/pressroom/presspacs/2023/october/mona-lisa-hides-a-surprising-mix-of-toxic-pigments.html used toxic pigments] when painting the ''[[wikipedia:Mona Lisa|Mona Lisa]]'', while his Japanese description mentions him losing his emotions, which could reference da Vinci's fascination with emotions and attempts to identify their source, and gaining knowledge of all kinds of comedy, just as da Vinci was versed in many fields of knowledge. They also have similar beards.
|-
|[[Prof. Owlbrowley]]
|[[wikipedia:Aleister Crowley|Aleister Crowley]] (English occultist and mystic)
|The "rowley" in Owlbrowley's name may be derived from Crowley. In this context, the abyss in their description may refer to the [[wikipedia:Abyss (Thelema)|Abyss]] from Crowley's religion [[wikipedia:Thelema|Thelema]].
|-
|[[Sage of Logic Newtone]]
|[[wikipedia:Isaac Newton|Isaac Newton]] (English polymath)
|Similar name and appearance. The apple he attacks with represents the apple that inspired Newton's gravitational theory, while his Slow ability and [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|allied self]]'s [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] target could possibly imply some form of gravity manipulation; ironically, he can be frozen by [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]]. During his attack animation, the movements made by the spheres he holds up mirror the movements made by the swinging spheres of a [[wikipedia:Newton's cradle|Newton's cradle]].<br>
Newtone's name may be a pun on ''Newton'' and ''stone'', which combined with his [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] trait could allude to the [[wikipedia:Philosopher's stone|philosopher's stone]], a legendary alchemical substance usually depicted as a red stone. [[wikipedia:Isaac Newton's occult studies#Alchemical research|Newton spent decades studying alchemy]] and is thought to have been pursuing the philosopher's stone.
|-
|[[Ange Lackey]]
|[[wikipedia:Babe Ruth|Babe Ruth]] (American baseball player)
|Like Babe Ruth, Ange Lackey is a revolutionary baseball player whose Japanese description says they excel at both pitching and batting, and their Japanese name, Enje Rūsu (エンジェ・ルース), can be taken as "Ange Luth" or "Ange Ruth". Their [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] trait may allude to how Babe Ruth was a lifelong Catholic who died wearing the [[wikipedia:Miraculous Medal|Miraculous Medal]], or ''[[wikipedia:The Babe Ruth Story|The Babe Ruth Story]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s exaggerated portrayal of Ruth as a literal miracle worker.
|-
|[[Sage of Selection Darvin]]
|[[wikipedia:Charles Darwin|Charles Darwin]] (English naturalist and evolutionary biologist)
|Similar name and beard. The giant tortoise is based on the [[wikipedia:Galápagos tortoise|Galápagos giant tortoise]], which contributed to Darwin's theory of evolution, while the primates on top represent human evolution, which Darwin discussed in ''[[wikipedia:The Descent of Man, and Selection in Relation to Sex|The Descent of Man, and Selection in Relation to Sex]]''.
