|[[wikipedia:Philosopher's stone|Philosopher's stone]] (mythical alchemical substance)
|The philosopher's stone's Japanese name, kenja no ishi (賢者の石), translates to "sage's stone", which may be why Sages are distinguished by a gemstone. Sages recovering from all debuffs more quickly is akin to the philosopher's stone curing any disease, and Sages like Techn-Old Hyena and Oldstrich being long-lived could be because it grants immortality.
|-
|[[Diabrollow]]
|[[wikipedia:Cronus|Cronus]] (Greek Titan)
|Diabrollow's Japanese name, Tsubasatān (ツバサターン), can be taken as "Tsubasaturn", as in [[wikipedia:Saturn (mythology)|Saturn]], a Roman deity conflated with Cronus. Diabrollow's wings resemble both scythes and jaws, referencing Cronus's use of a scythe and habit of swallowing his children; the Sage stone in its beak represents the stone that Cronus's sister-wife Rhea tricked him into swallowing instead of his sixth child, Zeus; Cronus was greedy for power, while Diabrollow is greedy for valuables; and Cronus is often confused with the god of time, [[wikipedia:Chronos|Chronos]], which could be referenced by Diabrollow appearing in [[Meeting of Long and Short]], the last stage of a [[A Journey of Moments|time-themed sub-chapter]].<br>Its [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] trait could come from  Cronus being banished to [[wikipedia:Tartarus|Tartarus]], a pit in the Underworld where the wicked are tormented, or to how ''Saturn'' sounds similar to ''Satan'' in Japanese; while its Sage type may refer to how [[wikipedia:Plato|Plato]] etymologized "Cronus" as roughly meaning "he of pure intellect", as described on [https://mythopedia.com/topics/cronus Mythopedia].
|-
|[[Sage of Life Dr. Nova]]
|[[wikipedia:List of tree deities|Tree deities]]
|Her design and [[Revival of Origin/Invasion|stage]] suggest influence from various tree deities, such as the [[wikipedia:Dryad|dryad]] and [[wikipedia:Hamadryad|hamadryad]] from Greek mythology. Her lower body being made up of green roots could also be a reference to the [https://www.dandwiki.com/wiki/Alraune_(5e_Race) alraune].
|-
| rowspan="3"|[[Prof. Owlbrowley]]
|[[wikipedia:Ascalaphus (son of Acheron)|Ascalaphus]] (Hades' orchardist-turned-owl)
|Ascalaphus was an orchardist of Hades whose name means "screech-owl". After he informed the other gods that Persephone had eaten pomegranate seeds in the Underworld, she was forced to spend part of each year there as Hades' wife. In turn, Ascalaphus was punished by either Persephone or Demeter by being pinned under a stone in the Underworld until he was freed by Heracles, after which the goddess turned him into a screech-owl, a sacred bird of Hades and herald of ill omen described by [[wikipedia:Ovid|Ovid]] as "the vilest bird; a messenger of grief; the lazy owl; sad omen to mankind." This is vaguely similar to how Prof. Owlbrowley put a [[wikipedia:Mortarboard|mortarboard]] with a Sage stone on their head, giving them knowledge of the underworld and turning them into a much more dishonorable professor who leads their students to doom. Their [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] trait may reference how Ascalaphus is literally the son of darkness—the name of his nymph mother, [[wikipedia:Orphne|Orphne]], means "darkness".
|-
|[[wikipedia:Owl of Athena|Owl of Athena]] (Greek symbol of wisdom)
|As a wise Sage and professor, Prof. Owbrowley could represent the Owl of Athena, a symbol of the goddess of wisdom and war. In contrast to her more violent brother Ares, Athena represents the tactics, strategy and intellectual side of war, which is somewhat shown in Owlbrowley's skill set compared to [[Owlbrow]]: instead of just dealing damage, they freeze units they hit, but have an uptime just short enough for those knocked back to re-enter their range and potentially get hit again.
|-
|[[wikia:mythus:Stolas|Stolas]] (demon from the ''[[wikipedia:Ars Goetia|Ars Goetia]]'')
|Prof. Owlbrowley's description and Sage type may have been inspired by Stolas, a wise Great Prince of Hell who is typically depicted as a owl and teaches knowledge of precious stones, as well as astronomy and herbs.
|-
|[[Shachiko]]
|[[wikipedia:Shachihoko|Shachihoko]] (Japanese sea monster)
|Shachiko's name may be derived from the two readings of the kanji 鯱: ''shachi'' ([[wikipedia:Orca|orca]]) and ''shachihoko''. This mythical creature has the head of a tiger and the body of a fish, which may be why Shachiko's Japanese description calls it a fish rather than a cetacean. Its ravenous appetite could come from how ''shachihoko'' are able to swallow massive amounts of water with a single gulp and hold it in their bellies.
|-
|[[Sage of Selection Darvin]]
|[[wikipedia:World Turtle|World Turtle]] (cosmological mytheme)
|The World Turtle is also known as the Cosmic Turtle, which may have inspired Darvin's [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] trait. The "tree of life" and man on his shell could specifically be based on the [[wikipedia:Turtle Island#Lenape|Lenape creation myth]], in which the first man and woman come from a tree grown on the turtle.<br>Darvin's "tree of life" may also be a nod to the [[wikipedia:World tree|world tree]], another cosmological mytheme.
|-
|[[Marquis Clionius]]
|[[wikipedia:Lilith|Lilith]] (Jewish demoness)
|Marquis Clionius' Japanese name, Kuorinesu Kyō (クオリネス), can be taken as "Lord Kuoliness" or "Lord Kuolineth", which may derive from クリオネ ''kurione'' ([[wikipedia:Clione|clione]]) and ''demoness'' or ''Lilith''. Marquis Clionius went from its home world to [[The Aku Realms]], is joined by three [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] children, and has katakana in its attack animation that translates to "cute children", while Lilith left the Garden of Eden and went on to bear many demonic children. Its debut sub-chapter appears to be about an obsessive person trying to force someone else into loving them and only them (see [[Yandere Chemistry#Trivia]] for more information), which could reference portrayals of Lilith as a succubus who seduces or even forces herself onto men, as in the [[wikipedia:Zohar|Zohar]].<br>Clionius' debut stage, [[Pipette of Passion]], appears to have been designed specifically for [[Lilith Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Queen Succubus Cat]], whose [[Talents]] were added in the same update as Clionius and whose Normal Form is named Lilith Cat in [[BCEN]]. Pipette of Passion and [[Distilled Devotion]] have [[Sinner Snache]], and Lilith has been associated with serpents, such as in ''[[wikipedia:Sistine Chapel ceiling#Adam_and_Eve|The Fall and Expulsion from Paradise]]'' on the Sistine Chapel ceiling, where the serpent in the Garden of Eden appears to be depicted as Lilith, and John Collier's painting ''[[wikipedia:Lilith (painting)|Lilith]]'', which shows a serpent coiled around her body.
|}

